Chapter: PlugExports
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 The wasm plug decides a module's EXPORTS by matching every definition name
 against `wasm-export-list`, a hardcoded pipe-separated string of about four
 hundred names taken from other applications -- `select-all`, `random-color`,
 `species-count`, `cad-set-units`. A program of this project's that happens to
 use one of those names is exported to the host whether it meant to be or not.

 Nothing here is wrong-answer; it is a surface question. The probe prints the
 same values either way, and what differs is the module's shape.

 We say:

Section: Entry

  select-all : Integer = 41
  random-color : Integer = 42
  species-count : Integer = 43

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("sum = " & show (select-all + random-color + species-count))
  end
